closed	p2	Backend stop/restart is very slow (~90s) on every deploy: uvicorn graceful-shutdown blocks on open SSE streams. Symptom: ansible 'fastapi_backend : Restart backend service' handler and plain 'systemctl stop new-archon-backend' hang for ~1.5min. ROOT CAUSE: on SIGTERM uvicorn stops accepting then waits (default timeout_graceful_shutdown=None = indefinitely) for active connections to finish, but the /stream SSE generators (main.py:509) are long-lived and never end on their own. The app DOES try to close them gracefully - lifespan-shutdown sets _shutdown_event + _wake_sse_connections() (main.py:372) and the SSE loop polls the event every <=1s (main.py:708-730) - BUT ASGI lifespan-shutdown runs only AFTER uvicorn has drained connections, i.e. after it is already blocked on those same streams, so the signal is too late. systemd then SIGKILLs at its default TimeoutStopSec=90s. service.j2:12 sets no --timeout-graceful-shutdown and the unit has no TimeoutStopSec/KillMode. FIXES to evaluate (prefer the first): (1) add uvicorn '--timeout-graceful-shutdown 5' to ExecStart so it force-closes lingering streams after a short grace instead of waiting forever; (2) install a SIGTERM handler that sets _shutdown_event immediately (before uvicorn starts draining) so streams self-close within ~1s; (3) systemd TimeoutStopSec=10 + KillMode=mixed as a backstop. Likely (1)+(2) together. Not a correctness bug (server does come back via Restart=always) - just makes every beta/prod deploy and manual restart slow. Affects #39 prod deploys too. Surfaced during #91 beta deploys. relates:#91 relates:#39
