closed	p1	Bot SSE listener wedges + loses missed transitions: processing each SSE event INLINE in the socket-read loop (sse_listener._sse_loop: await _dispatch_event inside async for resp.content) means any stalled handler await freezes stream consumption. On the beta a Discord handler stalled ~16:08 during the check-in-open announcement; the bot stopped reading, so the StartRound broadcast (and all later events) were never consumed — round 1 produced no seating message and no table voice channels, with NO error and NO reconnect (sock_read never fires while stuck in a handler, not at the read). Gateway/commands kept working (separate tasks) so /checkin still responded. Compounding bug: catch-up only SEEDS state (_handle_snapshot) and never replays missed transitions, so a reconnect/restart silently re-seeds rounds=1 and never creates the round-1 channels. FIX (both approved): (1) bound each _dispatch_event with asyncio.wait_for so no stall can wedge the listener; (2) make round/finals channel setup idempotent (check existing 'Table N'/'Finals' voice channels under the category) + reconcile on sync_complete so a (re)connect self-heals missing round channels. Note hikari REST total timeout is already 30s, so the 28-min wedge was a non-REST un-timed-out await — decoupling/bounding is the real fix, not a REST timeout. Surfaced in beta #91.
