closed	p2	Coalesce SSE queue frames per (type,uid) + lower maxsize. THE highest-value memory fix. Every tournament action rebroadcasts the WHOLE tournament object (~250-300KB for 400 players: players+rounds+standings+finals all inline, member projection strips only checkin_code/vekn_pushed_at) to all 400 connections (broadcast.py:128 broadcast_precomputed; tournaments.py:974). Frames are shared by reference so PROMPT drains are cheap, but a stalled queue (asyncio.Queue maxsize=100, broadcast.py:23) lets one slow phone accumulate 100x300KB=30MB before overflow->close fires. On congested venue WiFi 20-40 momentarily-stalled clients = 0.3-1.2GB transient = budget blown. Fix: make the per-connection queue keep only the LATEST frame per (type,uid) — successive whole-object snapshots of the same tournament supersede each other, so a stalled tournament viewer holds ~1 object (~300KB) not ~30MB (100x cut) and gets current state on drain instead of replaying 100 stale frames. Add maxsize 100->~20-30 as cheap insurance. parent:#197
